# When You Need More Control

Use `tf.function` and `get_concrete_function` to define explicit input shapes, then export.

```python
class MyModel(tf.keras.Model):
    @tf.function(input_signature=[tf.TensorSpec(shape=[None, 784], dtype=tf.float32)])
    def serve(self, x):
        return self(x)

model = MyModel()
# ... train
model.save('model_serving', signatures={'serving_default': model.serve})
```

This guarantees the server knows the exact input shape and dtype.
